course: dictionary
lesson: 1138
title: Breezy
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Breezy describes weather or a place where a light, fresh wind is blowing. «The Rat, used to a breezy river bedroom, feels sleepy and shut in.» The Rat is used to open, fresh air, so a breezy room is one with moving air.
explain: Look at the contrast in the sentence. The Mole feels lively underground, while the Rat feels sleepy and shut in. Shut in is the opposite of breezy, so breezy must mean fresh and open.
explain: Breezy can also describe a person's manner. A breezy manner is cheerful, relaxed and confident, sometimes too relaxed. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence, then try it in place of the word.
fact: Breezy means with a fresh wind blowing, as in «a breezy day».
fact: Breezy can also mean cheerful, relaxed and confident.
fact: Sometimes breezy means too relaxed, so the person may not be taking things seriously enough.
fact: A breezy day is windy but not stormy, which makes it good for flying kites and drying washing.
fact: The forms of breezy are breezy, breezier and breeziest.
exercise: «It was a breezy afternoon, perfect for flying a kite.» What does breezy mean here? | Dark and stormy | Frozen solid | Very hot and still | *With a fresh wind blowing
exercise: «The Rat, used to a breezy river bedroom, feels sleepy and shut in.» Why does the Rat feel shut in underground? | Because it is raining outside | Because he loves digging | *Because he is used to open, fresh air | Because he has too much food
exercise: «Ben is so breezy about his test.» What does breezy suggest about Ben? | Very nervous and shaky | Loud and angry | Fresh and windy | *Relaxed and confident, perhaps too relaxed
test: What does breezy mean in «a breezy manner»? | Heavy and wet | Cold and windy | *Cheerful, relaxed and confident | Quiet and sad
test: Which phrase best describes breezy weather? | *Windy but not stormy | Stormy and dangerous | Hot and dry, with no wind at all | Still and silent
exam: Which is the comparative form of breezy, as in «a breezier day»? | breezily | breezy | *breezier | breeziest
